/* core/data/trade.js -- window.AD_TRADE

   Export composition, top-5 exporter tables and revealed comparative
   advantage for the TRADLE / PICK 5 / CONNECTRADE cabinets.

   SOURCE  OEC olap-proxy (https://oec.world/api/olap-proxy/data.jsonrecords),
           cube trade_i_baci_a_92 = CEPII BACI, HS6 Rev. 1992, Year 2023.
           BACI is CEPII's mirror-reconciled rebuild of UN Comtrade; values
           are USD FOB. RCA is Balassa, computed locally from the same rows
           so shares and ranks in this file can never disagree.
   SCRIPT  _build/gen_trade.py  (re-runnable, deterministic, stdlib only)

   countries[] .i ISO2  .total USD  .hint one-liner
               .items[] {name, hs (HS2 chapter), share, colour}
               shares sum to 1 including the trailing "Other" remainder.
               .cov  basket / World Bank merchandise exports, same year.
               .note present ONLY when the basket is demonstrably partial
                     (under-reported to Comtrade, e.g. Iran) or is
                     re-export inflated. Surface it in the UI.
   top5[]      .hs4 .name .colour .n (how many countries export it at all)
               .world (world trade USD)
               .top  [[ISO2, USD]] for ranks 1..40, descending. Values are
                     4 significant figures, written short (1348e9), which is
                     legal JSON and reproduces every figure the game prints.
               .rest ranks 41+ as one flat string of 2-char ISO2 codes in rank
                     order, no values -- their exports are real but far too
                     small to score. Rank = 40 + index/2 + 1.
               PICK 5 scores a pick as value / sum(the FIRST FIVE values).
               .n = len(top) + len(rest)/2, so "#63 of 190" is exact.
               A country in NEITHER list really did export none of it in this
               year -- that is the only case where the game may say so. The
               median product here has 185 exporters out of the 226 countries
               this file can name, so "exports none" is almost always wrong.
   rca{ISO2}   6-9 products by revealed comparative advantage (Balassa),
               RCA-descending, each already filtered to >=0.5% of that
               country's exports (so the game never re-applies it).

     CONNECTRADE BOARD RULES -- follow both or you will ship broken days:
       1. Give each country the first FOUR of its products not already
          claimed by an earlier country in the board. The spare entries
          past four exist precisely to absorb those collisions.
       2. Allocate THINNEST LIST FIRST (ascending rca[c].length), then
          VALIDATE that you got 16 distinct products and redraw if not.
          Measured over 20,000 random 4-country boards: 99.87% solvable
          in draw order, 99.995% thinnest-first. The residue is real, not
          a data gap -- draw Libya + Brunei + Nigeria together and three
          petroleum economies genuinely cannot field 12 distinct exports.
          Redraw; do not paper over it.
   sections{}  HS section id -> {name, colour}; "0" = the Other remainder.
*/
